 "change": "OriginalApplicationBitmapInputs.observed runs in place (its checks first, then perform, which throws only before its first change: L5); the menu session's three call sites (observed, response, release) mutate its local bitmapInputs in place instead of a copy that was then assigned back. Each bitmap request of the front menu's construction copied the inputs' image, surface and DC tables up to twice.",
 "profile": "A12 launch profile (ml-ra-prof, sounds mixed): the game thread is on CPU 13.25 of 13.33 s to the loaded event; in the menu phase before the load (1-7 s) 53% of it builds the front menu's bitmaps (constructWithSurfaceLoading), with observed 7% and table copies and frees ~14%; the read-ahead threads use 1-2.5 of 8 cores.",
 "review": "Independent read-only review: OK, no defect (perform and observed throw before their first change; no catch inside the step sees leftover state; no overlapping access; the test's cases checked one by one).",
 "notes": "Gate phone A/B (warm-up first): launch to loaded 12.72-12.92 against 12.54-12.61 s, startup 1.65-1.86 against 1.50-1.57; a 4+4 A/B (ml-l20-ab4) overlaps: launch to loaded 12.54-12.71 (median 12.62) against 12.59-13.17 (12.67), menu phase 4.92-5.30 (5.15) against 5.24-5.52 (5.35), load 5.74-6.11 against 5.49-6.03, startup 1.53-1.66 against 1.51-1.86. The menu phase is shorter but the loading step then waits longer for the read-ahead, which ends ~6 s after startup in both builds (the phone under memory pressure): the read-ahead, not the menu, is the critical path now. Mac neutral (menu phase 0.31-0.33 s both). Frame time overlapping (main 10.36-10.48 against 10.29-10.43 ms per tick).",
